According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Green Cleaning Products market was valued at USD 13.2 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 23.1 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 5.6% during the forecast period (2026–2034). This growth is driven by tightening regulatory frameworks on hazardous chemicals, an accelerating consumer shift toward healthier indoor environments, and expanding corporate sustainability programmes that favour eco friendly janitorial solutions.
Green cleaning products are formulations that rely on biodegradable surfactants, plant based solvents, enzyme systems and low toxicity additives to achieve high level hygiene while minimizing environmental footprints. By substituting petrochemical derived ingredients with renewable raw materials such as citrus terpenes, coconut derived fatty acids and microbial enzymes, these solutions curb volatile organic compound (VOC) emissions, preserve aquatic ecosystems and improve safety for occupants in residential, commercial and institutional settings.
